        <nav class="breadcrumb reveal"><a href="index.html">Home</a> / <a href="kenya.html">Kenya</a> / Nairobi &amp; Giraffe Manor</nav>
        <p class="article__lead reveal">Most safaris begin and end in Nairobi — and it's worth more than a layover. Kenya's capital is green, creative and surprisingly wild, with a national park on its doorstep, baby elephants to meet, and giraffes that may join you for breakfast.</p>

        <h2 class="reveal">Giraffe Manor</h2>
        <p class="reveal">The famous boutique hotel where resident Rothschild's giraffes poke their heads through the windows at breakfast. It books up far ahead — we secure dates and pair it with a wider Kenya journey.</p>

        <h2 class="reveal">The Sheldrick Elephant Orphanage</h2>
        <p class="reveal">The Sheldrick Wildlife Trust rescues and rehabilitates orphaned elephants. A visit to watch the babies at their mud bath — and learn about conservation — is moving and a highlight for families.</p>

        <h2 class="reveal">Nairobi National Park</h2>
        <p class="reveal">The only national park within a capital city: lions, rhino and giraffe roam against a skyline backdrop. A perfect half-day safari before or after your flight.</p>

        <h2 class="reveal">Food, culture &amp; shopping</h2>
        <p class="reveal">From farm-to-table restaurants and rooftop bars to the Maasai Market and women-led craft collectives, Nairobi rewards a day or two of slow exploring.</p>

        <h2 class="reveal">Is Nairobi safe for women travellers?</h2>
        <p class="reveal">With sensible precautions, yes. We use trusted hotels and private, vetted drivers throughout, with a concierge on call — so you can enjoy the city with confidence.</p>

        <h2 class="reveal">Where to stay &amp; getting around</h2>
        <p class="reveal">We book women-friendly boutique hotels and arrange all private transfers from Jomo Kenyatta International Airport. Nairobi is the hub for flights to every park.</p>

